  "brief": "<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Market Overview</h2>\n\nMixed pre-market action with SPY grinding higher at $757.61 (+0.15%) while small caps lag with IWM down -0.32%. VIX spike to 24.43 (+1.20%) signals underlying tension despite NASDAQ leading at +0.55% on tech strength. Clear rotation into defensive growth plays as geopolitical risk escalates.\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> What to Watch</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>ISM Manufacturing PMI (2:00 PM ET)</strong> - May's reading will set tone for industrial sector after weak pre-market performance</li>\n<li><strong>Iran-Israel Tensions</strong> - Hormuz Strait blockade threats could spike oil and tank risk assets</li>\n<li><strong>UAW Strike</strong> - GM truck production under threat, watch industrials and auto suppliers</li>\n<li><strong>Jobs Report Expectations</strong> - Kalshi traders betting on May payrolls beat, could influence Fed pricing</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Sector Rotation</h2>\n\nClear flight to quality tech names with XLK up +2.33% and energy catching a geopolitical bid at +1.90%. Consumer discretionary getting hammered (-2.16%) alongside utilities, signaling economic growth concerns. Classic risk-off rotation with defensive tech replacing cyclicals.\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-green\"><div class=\"callout-label\">✦ Bull Case</div>NVIDIA and mega-cap tech continue to eclipse macro concerns. May jobs beat could confirm soft landing narrative and fuel summer rally.</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-red\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚠ Bear Case</div>Iran threatens Hormuz closure while VIX spikes suggest options flow turning defensive. Consumer discretionary breakdown signals demand destruction ahead.</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-amber\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚡ Key Driver</div>ISM Manufacturing at 2:00 PM ET. Sub-50 reading with weak employment component could trigger broader industrial selloff.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Levels That Matter</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SPY 755</strong> - Key support from Friday's close, break targets 750 quickly</li>\n<li><strong>QQQ 745</strong> - Resistance from overnight high, clear run to 750+ if taken</li>\n<li><strong>VIX 25</strong> - Next resistance level, break signals real fear trade incoming</li>\n<li><strong>XLE 95</strong> - Energy sector breakout level if Iran situation escalates</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr>\n<p><em>Not a prediction. A preparation. Make your plan before the bell.</em></p>",
